The mockups are not committed here.

They live in the Claude Design project this design drop came from:

    project: "UI mockups and scoping"
    id:      ac18593f-81b1-4150-bf31-4f0e15863e26
    url:     https://claude.ai/design/p/ac18593f-81b1-4150-bf31-4f0e15863e26

    PICKsel Phase 1 - Golden Path.dc.html      S1.1 – S1.9
    PICKsel Phase 2 - Auditors World.dc.html   S2.1 – S2.7
    PICKsel Phase 3 - Clients World.dc.html    S3.1 – S3.6
    PICKsel Phase 4 - Running the Network.dc.html
    PICKsel Phase 5 - Onboarding.dc.html

Claude Code reads them on demand with the claude-design MCP (`read_file`),
which is the same source design/manifest.md is generated from.

Why not committed: 110 KB of entity-escaped HTML copied through a chat
context is a spec we build against, and a mangled or stale copy is worse
than no local copy. Drop the real files in when there is a reason to —
offline review, or diffing a new drop against the last one — and delete
this file.

This directory is kept so the paths in design/README.md and design/manifest.md
resolve to something that explains itself.
